[08:12:38] Playbook updated from 3 viral Shorts:
[08:12:38]   - Hook with an immediate visual shock or a relatable scam/myth rather than corporate announcements or brand press releases.
[08:12:38]   - Introduce the core conflict or tension within the first 1 to 5 seconds; never spend the opening lines describing product specs.
[08:12:38]   - Make numbers feelable using everyday tangible comparisons rather than abstract high-level concepts.
[08:12:38]   - Structure long shorts (60-90s) as an active test, experiment, or step-by-step problem debunk rather than a monologue lecture.
[08:12:38]   - If producing short-form spectacle (15-20s), eliminate spoken voiceover entirely and rely purely on immersive natural sound and clear visual scale.
[08:12:38]   - Keep language strictly simple and conversational; completely ban abstract pseudo-philosophical questions.
[08:12:38]   - End the script abruptly on the punchline, critical payoff, or definitive result without rolling into generic outro questions.
[08:12:38]   - Keep overall length intentionally binary: either ultra-tight 15-20s visual spectacles or 60-85s narrative investigations, avoiding mid-length dragging.
[08:12:38]   - Space out dialogue to maintain breathing room; do not exceed 2.6 words per second to prevent cognitive overload.
